# ---- a triage session that keeps failing (optional — 3 is the default) ----
# TRIAGE_FAIL_CONSUME_AFTER is how many CONSECUTIVE rc!=0 triage sessions on the
# SAME board fingerprint the tick pays for before it consumes that fingerprint
# anyway and alerts once (id triage-fail-consume:<project>). Without it a lane
# whose session dies every time re-buys the identical failure on every cron tick:
# project-5 billed 1,168 rc!=0 triage rows in one day on one fingerprint.
#   3   = the default: three attempts, then stop paying and say so.
#   1   = consume on the first failure.
#   0   = never consume on failure (the behaviour this replaced).
# A success clears the count; a changed board fingerprint restarts it at 1. A
# blank or non-numeric value reads as 3, never as "no cap".
#TRIAGE_FAIL_CONSUME_AFTER=3

